# Puppet – Short Command Notes

Setup: Two Debian 13 machines.

- Puppet Server: Stores manifests and controls configuration.
- Puppet Agent: Connects to the server and applies configurations.

### 1. Set hostnames

Run on Puppet Server:

```
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname puppet-server
```

Run on Puppet Agent:

```
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname puppet-agent
```

### 2. Configure name resolution

Run on both machines:

```
sudo nano /etc/hosts
```

Add:

```
SERVER_PRIVATE_IP puppet-server
AGENT_PRIVATE_IP puppet-agent
```

### 3. Install Puppet repository

Run on both machines:

```
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y wget
wget https://apt.puppet.com/puppet8-release-trixie.deb
sudo dpkg -i puppet8-release-trixie.deb
sudo apt update
```

### 4. Install Puppet Server

Run on Puppet Server:

```
sudo apt install -y puppetserver
```

### 5. Install Puppet Agent

Run on Puppet Agent:

```
sudo apt install -y puppet-agent
```

### 6. Configure Puppet Server

Run on Puppet Server:

```
sudo nano /etc/puppetlabs/puppet/puppet.conf
```

Add:

```
[main]
certname = puppet-server
server = puppet-server
```

Start Puppet Server:

```
sudo systemctl enable --now puppetserver
sudo systemctl status puppetserver
```

### 7. Configure Puppet Agent

Run on Puppet Agent:

```
sudo nano /etc/puppetlabs/puppet/puppet.conf
```

Add:

```
[main]
certname = puppet-agent
server = puppet-server
```

### 8. Request Agent Certificate

Run on Puppet Agent:

```
sudo /opt/puppetlabs/bin/puppet agent --test
```

### 9. Sign Agent Certificate

Run on Puppet Server:

```
sudo /opt/puppetlabs/bin/puppetserver ca list
sudo /opt/puppetlabs/bin/puppetserver ca sign --certname puppet-agent
```

### 10. Create Puppet Manifest

Run on Puppet Server:

```
sudo nano /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/production/manifests/site.pp
```

Add:

```
node 'puppet-agent' {
  package { 'apache2':
    ensure => installed,
  }

  service { 'apache2':
    ensure  => running,
    enable  => true,
    require => Package['apache2'],
  }

  file { '/var/www/html/index.html':
    ensure  => file,
    content => 'Apache configured using Puppet!',
    require => Package['apache2'],
  }
}
```

### 11. Apply Manifest

Run on Puppet Agent:

```
sudo /opt/puppetlabs/bin/puppet agent --test
```

### 12. Verify Apache

Run on Puppet Agent:

```
sudo systemctl status apache2
curl http://localhost
```

Browser:

```
http://AGENT_PRIVATE_IP
```

